1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,730
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:17,980
If you want to be my sugar baby…

6
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:19,880
You are mine only.

7
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:23,300
But it doesn’t mean
that I will have only you.

8
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:25,850
You need to help me get Chan back.

9
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:28,200
Otherwise, I won’t help you
with the debt you owe me.

10
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,650
Hi.

11
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,000
Do you miss me?

12
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,920
From now on, making you smile

13
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,700
will be my main duty.

14
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:39,200
Who is this girl?

15
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,810
Just say what you want to say.

16
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:02,370
Come on, sis.

17
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:04,400
Why are you in such a hurry?

18
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:08,600
I just want to get to know your girl.

19
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:16,400
Please take good care of my sister.

20
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:22,080
She can be stern, hotheaded,
and irritable sometimes.

21
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:26,100
But she’s actually a sweet person.

22
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:30,250
No matter what she is like,

23
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:32,500
I can handle her.

24
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:35,000
She has the confidence.

25
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,160
I like her.

26
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:40,610
This is the kind of girl
who can handle you.

27
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:42,800
Sister.

28
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,050
You have my approval.

29
00:01:47,630 --> 00:01:48,700
Thank you.

30
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,930
I’ll do my best.

31
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,370
You should leave.

32
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,100
Don’t try to get rid of me.

33
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,250
What do you want to talk to me about?

34
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,500
I came to see you today

35
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:15,560
because I want to talk to you about Jay.

36
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:24,760
I think she wants to get back with you.

37
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:34,600
But I don’t want it to happen.

38
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:40,300
Can you promise me
that you won’t get back with her?

39
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,090
Aren’t you hurt enough because of her?

40
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:52,920
Can you stop talking about her, Sun?

41
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,870
No.

42
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,120
I won’t stop.

43
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:58,280
I don’t want to see you
falling apart again.

44
00:02:58,530 --> 00:02:59,440
Sun.

45
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:06,800
You should leave.

46
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:16,760
You too.

47
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,000
I want to be alone tonight.

48
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,720
How long are you going to stay, Miss?

49
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:13,750
Indefinitely.

50
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,750
It’s our pleasure.

51
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,100
What are you doing here?

52
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:49,500
I just want to try your hotel service.

53
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,150
Your hotel is the best, right?

54
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,000
You should stay at another hotel.

55
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,000
I’ll arrange it for you.

56
00:06:00,490 --> 00:06:01,400
No.

57
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,450
I’m going to stay here.

58
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,700
I don’t know what you are planning.

59
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:10,640
But it’s not going to happen.

60
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:25,400
You can’t run away from me, Chan.

61
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:29,600
I’m going to get back with you.

62
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:34,450
You and I can never really be over.

63
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:42,400
I’m asking you.

64
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,900
Don’t cause a problem at my hotel.

65
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:51,500
I’m not here to cause a problem.

66
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:56,200
I stay here because of work.

67
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:01,180
I want to monitor the restaurant
to make sure everything is in order.

68
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:02,510
Okay?

69
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,850
Is that all?

70
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:15,700
Okay.

71
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:20,390
Welcome to the Crescent.

72
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:50,900
Jay.

73
00:07:51,610 --> 00:07:53,440
Don’t you think
you’re coming on a little too strong?

74
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,320
You are making Chan uncomfortable.

75
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:04,400
You know her well.

76
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:07,960
If I don’t do this,
I will never get her back.

77
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:15,500
From now on, I’ll discuss the details
of the restaurant opening with Chan.

78
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:19,000
You just set up a meeting with her for me.

79
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:20,700
But this is also my restaurant.

80
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,210
I want to attend the meeting as well.

81
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:23,700
Sorry.

82
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,600
You don’t need to attend it.

83
00:08:25,650 --> 00:08:26,880
Just make an appointment for me.

84
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,560
You can go now.

85
00:08:37,419 --> 00:08:39,640
I’ll hurry to pay you back
as soon as possible.

86
00:08:40,039 --> 00:08:43,700
When I fully pay you back,
just so we’re clear,

87
00:08:45,550 --> 00:08:47,300
I will not help you with Chan anymore.

88
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:51,580
If Chan refuses to get back with you,

89
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,760
I want you to move on.

90
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,500
Don’t worry about that.

91
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:03,580
I will make her love me again.

92
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:52,700
Can I drink it too?

93
00:09:52,770 --> 00:09:53,600
Jay.

94
00:09:54,190 --> 00:09:55,560
Why are you that surprised?

95
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:58,800
You suddenly pop up. So I’m taken aback.

96
00:09:59,160 --> 00:09:59,980
Can I?

97
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,500
Sure. You can drink it first.

98
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:05,240
I mean, we should drink it together.

99
00:10:06,330 --> 00:10:07,300
How?

100
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:10,200
You drink it first.

101
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,600
Come on.

102
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:07,520
(Hurry up.)

103
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:10,100
(You know what.)

104
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:12,800
(I thought you liked boys.)

105
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:16,300
(Because of you,)

106
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:19,000
(I realized that I like girls.)

107
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:27,800
(What if one day I change my mind
and like a boy?)

108
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:32,880
It’s okay.

109
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:38,800
(As long as you like me right now,
that's enough for me.)

110
00:12:11,430 --> 00:12:12,800
Chan, it’s time to move on.

111
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:15,700
Don’t be a fool.

112
00:12:42,410 --> 00:12:43,600
Can you come to see me?

113
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:23,970
Thank you for buying me
an entire new wardrobe.

114
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,300
No need to thank me.

115
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:28,200
You are my sugar baby.

116
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,600
It’s too bad.

117
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,300
The shop doesn’t sell nightgowns.

118
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:35,400
Right?

119
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:38,700
Nightgowns.

120
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:41,450
I don’t think you need them.

121
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:44,100
You’re right.

122
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,780
I don’t need them.

123
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,500
You’re such a perv.

124
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:56,500
Didn’t you say you’re changing
my fashion style?

125
00:13:57,390 --> 00:13:59,200
Don’t my nightgowns
need to be changed too?

126
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,580
You should go to work.

127
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:04,840
You’ll be late.

128
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:09,800
Aren’t you going to watch me sing tonight?

129
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:12,800
No.

130
00:14:13,370 --> 00:14:16,360
I've reached my limit
for spending time with people for today.

131
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:23,450
Where am I going to put those clothes?

132
00:14:24,310 --> 00:14:28,000
I can take them to my condo first.

133
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:32,000
I can move in with you.

134
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,300
So I don’t have to
take them back to my home.

135
00:14:41,470 --> 00:14:42,700
You should go to work.

136
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,900
Alright.

137
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,500
Thank you so much.

138
00:14:48,010 --> 00:14:49,500
I had a great time today.

139
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:56,900
Bye.

140
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:17,010
♪ The way you touch me here tonight ♪

141
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:21,250
♪ Makes my feelings come alive ♪

142
00:15:21,650 --> 00:15:25,450
♪ When you come close
I hear your heartbeat ♪

143
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:29,700
♪ My heart is racing, feeling the heat ♪

144
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:32,030
♪ You tell me I should never kiss you ♪

145
00:15:32,070 --> 00:15:34,060
♪ Scared it could get dangerous ♪

146
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,010
♪ But every time you tell me no ♪

147
00:15:36,050 --> 00:15:38,520
♪ You only make me lose control ♪

148
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:43,010
♪ Let every rhythm, yours and mine ♪

149
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:46,830
♪ Move in sync,
let our hearts come alive ♪

150
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:51,400
♪ The closer we get,
I can’t resist a kiss ♪

151
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:55,000
♪ Just follow what you feel, my Red Kiss ♪

152
00:15:55,110 --> 00:16:03,000
♪ Let this be the rhythm,
yours and mine, ohh ♪

153
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:07,760
♪ The closer we are,
I can’t resist a kiss ♪

154
00:16:07,890 --> 00:16:11,170
♪ Just follow what you feel, my Red Kiss ♪

155
00:16:12,870 --> 00:16:16,100
Why are you so dressed up today, Key?

156
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:18,250
Someone bought me this dress.

157
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:20,800
Someone bought it for you?

158
00:16:21,510 --> 00:16:22,800
Who?

159
00:16:23,590 --> 00:16:24,400
Hold on.

160
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:27,880
You never let anyone tell you
what to wear.

161
00:16:28,510 --> 00:16:29,900
Why are you letting her do that?

162
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:31,100
Look at her.

163
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:33,210
I guess you are serious about this one.

164
00:16:34,490 --> 00:16:36,600
Stop teasing me.

165
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:40,930
Don’t you have to go home?
Won’t your partner call looking for you?

166
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:42,400
I’m not going home.

167
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:44,380
I need to get all the tea on you first.

168
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,400
What?

169
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,300
So?

170
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:51,800
Are you going to listen to my tea?

171
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,200
Or go home?

172
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,490
Fine, I’ve got to go.

173
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,170
Why? Are you afraid of your girlfriend?

174
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,100
No.

175
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:01,400
-I’m leaving.
-Me too.

176
00:17:01,850 --> 00:17:03,000
See you.

177
00:17:12,089 --> 00:17:13,800
You are a talented singer.

178
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:16,880
Hi.

179
00:17:17,569 --> 00:17:18,599
Have a seat.

180
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:26,099
We run into each other quite often,
as you said.

181
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:30,100
Don’t you think
we should tell each other our names?

182
00:17:30,810 --> 00:17:33,040
No, I like it this way.

183
00:17:35,210 --> 00:17:37,810
Do you like things to be mysterious?

184
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:39,400
It’s fun.

185
00:17:41,930 --> 00:17:43,970
You are afraid that
you will fall for me, aren’t you?

186
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,250
No.

187
00:17:50,210 --> 00:17:51,330
Are you worried about that?

188
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:55,900
No, I already have someone I like.

189
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:57,800
What about you?

190
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,050
Do you have one?

191
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,900
Yes.

192
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:07,100
But there’s a problem.

193
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,300
She is really mad at me.

194
00:18:21,390 --> 00:18:22,600
But it’s my fault.

195
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:28,400
Why don’t you try to make up with her?

196
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:30,790
I’m trying.

197
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:34,640
But it’s very hard.

198
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:46,200
If you can’t move on from her,

199
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:51,300
you need to do everything

200
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,530
so you can go on with her.

201
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,920
Even if it means
you need to change yourself,

202
00:19:05,070 --> 00:19:06,200
you need to do it.

203
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,960
So you can be with her.

204
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:18,900
If I can’t be myself, is that a good idea?

205
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:24,170
It’s the price you have to pay.

206
00:19:27,210 --> 00:19:28,600
Sometimes,

207
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,180
for love,

208
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,100
we have to do it.

209
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:38,730
I like what you said.

210
00:19:43,710 --> 00:19:44,700
I get it now.

211
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,480
I’m rooting for you.

212
00:20:03,650 --> 00:20:04,500
Hello.

213
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:07,000
Right now?

214
00:20:07,830 --> 00:20:08,570
Sure.

215
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,100
I’ll be right there.

216
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:16,900
I’ve got to go.

217
00:20:18,770 --> 00:20:20,090
I’m rooting for you.

218
00:20:22,010 --> 00:20:22,800
Bye.

219
00:20:23,470 --> 00:20:24,400
Good luck.

220
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:48,700
Can you give me another chance, Chan?

221
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:04,200
Chan, I’m here.

222
00:21:08,910 --> 00:21:09,900
Chan.

223
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:28,300
Are you playing hide-and-seek with me,
pretty sis?

224
00:21:34,010 --> 00:21:35,100
Chan.

225
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:40,780
Chan.

226
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:45,100
You got caught, little perv.

227
00:21:48,730 --> 00:21:50,380
You caught me.

228
00:21:51,930 --> 00:21:54,200
What are you going to do to me?

229
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,900
I will…

230
00:22:00,670 --> 00:22:01,880
give you a penalty.

231
00:22:12,770 --> 00:22:14,600
Do you want me to take a shower first?

232
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:23,370
You still smell good.

233
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:47,400
Chan.

234
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:52,100
Jay.

235
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:03,090
How did you get in here?

236
00:23:21,030 --> 00:23:21,950
You.

237
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:23,980
You…

238
00:23:26,490 --> 00:23:28,330
You are Chan’s ex?

239
00:23:33,070 --> 00:23:33,900
Chan.

240
00:23:35,530 --> 00:23:37,010
Is she your new girlfriend?

241
00:23:39,180 --> 00:23:40,400
She’s not my girlfriend.

242
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:49,400
It’s complicated.

243
00:23:50,710 --> 00:23:52,200
How did you get in?

244
00:23:54,340 --> 00:23:56,210
You gave me your keycard.

245
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:57,570
I’ve never thrown it away.

246
00:24:02,270 --> 00:24:05,960
So what is your relationship with her?

247
00:24:10,930 --> 00:24:12,200
She’s just my sugar baby.

248
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:21,700
Now I get it

249
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:25,370
why I don’t want to tell you my name.

250
00:24:32,030 --> 00:24:34,100
I don’t think we can be friends.

251
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,240
Did you meet Key before?

252
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,730
So your name is Key.

253
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,000
You should leave.

254
00:24:51,310 --> 00:24:52,770
I want to talk to my girlfriend.

255
00:25:03,020 --> 00:25:04,790
Didn’t you break up?

256
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:08,930
What right do you have
to tell me to leave?

257
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:12,700
Right now,

258
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:18,540
Chan is no longer your girlfriend.

259
00:25:18,580 --> 00:25:20,040
Neither are you.

260
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,400
That’s enough.

261
00:25:24,870 --> 00:25:25,900
Both of you.

262
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,100
Chan.

263
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:40,600
You and I need to talk.

264
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:44,700
You have no right to tell me what to do.

265
00:25:47,580 --> 00:25:48,700
We broke up.

266
00:25:49,530 --> 00:25:50,700
Don’t you remember?

267
00:25:53,310 --> 00:25:54,300
You should leave.

268
00:26:09,980 --> 00:26:10,900
I’ll see you.

269
00:26:25,950 --> 00:26:27,000
You should leave too.

270
00:26:30,790 --> 00:26:31,290
But…

271
00:26:31,330 --> 00:26:32,500
You have no right.

272
00:26:35,540 --> 00:26:37,320
Don’t forget your status.

273
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:36,560
KEY

274
00:27:46,670 --> 00:27:47,600
Come in.

275
00:28:03,040 --> 00:28:03,770
Miss Chan.

276
00:28:04,860 --> 00:28:06,290
Mr. Phu is here to see you.

277
00:28:15,250 --> 00:28:16,100
Please come in.

278
00:28:34,620 --> 00:28:35,400
Chan.

279
00:28:36,850 --> 00:28:37,900
I’m sorry.

280
00:28:39,580 --> 00:28:41,080
I shouldn’t have asked Jay for help.

281
00:28:41,110 --> 00:28:42,200
It’s too late, Phu.

282
00:28:42,610 --> 00:28:43,500
Let it slide.

283
00:28:44,990 --> 00:28:46,370
I’m not mad at you about that.

284
00:28:48,050 --> 00:28:51,400
I’m mad at you
because when you have a problem,

285
00:28:52,210 --> 00:28:53,600
you never come to me.

286
00:28:55,670 --> 00:28:59,160
I didn’t want you
to be disappointed in me.

287
00:28:59,850 --> 00:29:03,760
But you are disappointing me right now.

288
00:29:10,890 --> 00:29:11,700
Forget it.

289
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:16,300
You need to do everything

290
00:29:17,410 --> 00:29:18,970
to make Jay leave this hotel.

291
00:29:23,650 --> 00:29:24,800
That’s the problem.

292
00:29:25,810 --> 00:29:30,400
Jay told me
she needs to see you right now.

293
00:29:32,510 --> 00:29:34,160
She gave me an ultimatum.

294
00:29:35,030 --> 00:29:36,900
You need to go to see her.

295
00:29:43,790 --> 00:29:45,200
She will leave…

296
00:29:46,820 --> 00:29:49,180
only when you tell her to leave.

297
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:54,500
She will not leave, Phu.

298
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,320
Never.

299
00:30:30,660 --> 00:30:31,850
What’s wrong, little rascal?

300
00:30:32,900 --> 00:30:34,300
Why aren’t you eating?

301
00:30:34,650 --> 00:30:35,970
You’re looking so down.

302
00:30:37,490 --> 00:30:38,700
It’s nothing.

303
00:30:39,180 --> 00:30:40,300
I’m okay.

304
00:30:40,750 --> 00:30:41,980
You’re okay?

305
00:30:42,370 --> 00:30:44,920
You’re so not okay.

306
00:30:47,230 --> 00:30:48,800
I’m really okay, Peach.

307
00:30:49,610 --> 00:30:50,700
I swear.

308
00:30:51,070 --> 00:30:51,920
You’re lying.

309
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:54,600
I’m not lying.

310
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:03,240
When you lie, you always avoid
looking me in the eye.

311
00:31:03,910 --> 00:31:05,000
I’m not doing that.

312
00:31:05,980 --> 00:31:06,920
Will you tell me or not?

313
00:31:08,610 --> 00:31:09,400
Huh?

314
00:31:11,730 --> 00:31:13,130
Fine, I’ll tell you.

315
00:31:18,550 --> 00:31:21,200
I’m so tired of how you catch me lying.

316
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:25,390
I’ve been using this method
since you were five.

317
00:31:25,430 --> 00:31:26,560
It always works.

318
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,000
This is cheating.

319
00:31:28,400 --> 00:31:31,400
You can't tell anyone about it.
Otherwise, I’ll be mad at you.

320
00:31:32,530 --> 00:31:33,580
I won’t tell anyone.

321
00:31:34,370 --> 00:31:36,160
So I can have all the fun to myself.

322
00:31:36,820 --> 00:31:39,700
But you told Dad, Big Mom, and Aunt Niam.

323
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:42,900
Alright.

324
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:46,410
So what is your problem?

325
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,600
Why did you cry?

326
00:31:51,290 --> 00:31:53,200
How did you know I cried?

327
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:56,000
Your eyes are all swollen.

328
00:31:56,310 --> 00:31:59,500
Anyone can tell
that you were crying all night.

329
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,100
Do you want some wine?

330
00:32:25,730 --> 00:32:27,320
Can you stop doing this?

331
00:32:30,100 --> 00:32:31,500
Doing this?

332
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:32,630
Doing what?

333
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:34,480
You always have to get things your way.

334
00:32:39,470 --> 00:32:42,500
You know me well.

335
00:32:50,550 --> 00:32:51,580
I’m asking you.

336
00:32:53,020 --> 00:32:54,400
Please leave my hotel.

337
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:55,700
I won’t leave

338
00:32:57,790 --> 00:32:59,400
until you get back with me.

339
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:01,090
Do you think doing this
will help you get me back?

340
00:33:11,130 --> 00:33:15,300
You know I don’t care about methods.

341
00:33:17,690 --> 00:33:19,240
All I care about is the result.

342
00:33:21,260 --> 00:33:23,600
I will do everything to get you back.

343
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:41,600
I really miss you, you know?

344
00:33:52,270 --> 00:33:53,900
We broke up a long time ago, Jay.

345
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,200
Please don’t do this.

346
00:34:07,680 --> 00:34:09,280
But I’m back now.

347
00:34:12,710 --> 00:34:14,000
I came back to you.

348
00:34:17,070 --> 00:34:18,840
I will never leave again.

349
00:34:20,380 --> 00:34:21,280
I promise.

350
00:34:29,270 --> 00:34:31,600
We will go back to how we were before.

351
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:42,699
Walk slowly.

352
00:34:43,690 --> 00:34:44,600
A little further.

353
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:46,699
A bit further.

354
00:34:46,780 --> 00:34:47,690
Can I open my eyes now?

355
00:34:47,730 --> 00:34:48,550
Three.

356
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:50,400
Two.

357
00:34:51,870 --> 00:34:52,760
One.

358
00:35:02,550 --> 00:35:05,800
You bought me a piano.

359
00:35:07,290 --> 00:35:08,900
Why did you do that?

360
00:35:09,370 --> 00:35:14,200
I bought it to show how much I love you.

361
00:35:21,200 --> 00:35:22,200
Thank you.

362
00:35:27,650 --> 00:35:29,000
(I promise)

363
00:35:29,690 --> 00:35:32,500
(I will take good care of your piano.)

364
00:35:33,130 --> 00:35:34,300
Of course, I like it.

365
00:35:34,850 --> 00:35:36,300
(It’s not my piano.)

366
00:35:37,770 --> 00:35:39,000
It’s our piano.

367
00:35:42,990 --> 00:35:44,500
It sounds amazing.

368
00:35:45,690 --> 00:35:46,800
Thank you.

369
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:50,200
I love you so much.

370
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:13,000
You are my first love, Chan.

371
00:36:32,990 --> 00:36:33,800
Chan.

372
00:36:35,990 --> 00:36:37,120
You’re up?

373
00:36:38,370 --> 00:36:39,800
Did I wake you up?

374
00:36:40,050 --> 00:36:41,600
You need to take responsibility for it.

375
00:36:41,730 --> 00:36:42,600
Hold me.

376
00:36:42,610 --> 00:36:43,400
Come here.

377
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,100
Jay.

378
00:37:01,890 --> 00:37:03,100
I’m home.

379
00:37:04,970 --> 00:37:06,700
I bought snacks for you.

380
00:37:16,190 --> 00:37:17,000
Jay.

381
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:42,350
I'M SORRY.
—J.

382
00:38:06,350 --> 00:38:09,300
It’s true that we are
each other’s first love.

383
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:16,000
For me,

384
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:20,500
our relationship ended a long time ago.

385
00:38:32,110 --> 00:38:33,200
I can’t accept it.

386
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:41,000
I know you still love me.

387
00:38:43,550 --> 00:38:45,200
You can’t run away from me, Chan.

388
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:49,600
You can’t run away from your feelings.

389
00:38:57,520 --> 00:38:59,170
Please give me another chance.

390
00:39:06,500 --> 00:39:07,450
Please.

391
00:39:36,910 --> 00:39:38,100
I’m sorry.

392
00:39:39,370 --> 00:39:40,100
No.

393
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:44,900
I’m sorry.

394
00:39:49,340 --> 00:39:50,600
No, please.

395
00:39:56,570 --> 00:39:57,300
Please

396
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:38,300
Peach.

397
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:41,500
Please say something.

398
00:40:43,260 --> 00:40:44,800
What do you want me to say?

399
00:40:47,330 --> 00:40:48,800
Don’t worry, Peach.

400
00:40:49,630 --> 00:40:51,100
How can I not be worried?

401
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:54,700
What are you thinking?

402
00:40:55,780 --> 00:40:57,580
Why did you agree to be her sugar baby?

403
00:40:58,170 --> 00:41:01,240
If Dad and Big Mom find out,
they will be crushed.

404
00:41:02,640 --> 00:41:04,000
Then don’t tell them.

405
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:06,500
Please, Peach.

406
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:10,880
Why are you doing this, Key?

407
00:41:13,980 --> 00:41:16,000
You agreed to be Chan’s sugar baby.

408
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:18,370
Is it because of Mom?

409
00:41:23,810 --> 00:41:24,800
No.

410
00:41:25,060 --> 00:41:26,240
You’re lying.

411
00:41:27,790 --> 00:41:28,970
You are doing this

412
00:41:29,890 --> 00:41:33,300
because you think
you don’t deserve her, don’t you?

413
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:39,050
Key.

414
00:41:40,350 --> 00:41:41,990
You are my sister.

415
00:41:43,750 --> 00:41:46,000
For me, you are very important.

416
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:49,090
Everyone in our family
also feels the same way.

417
00:41:53,530 --> 00:41:54,500
I know.

418
00:41:56,510 --> 00:41:57,700
But I…

419
00:41:59,380 --> 00:42:01,100
I don’t feel confident.

420
00:42:28,610 --> 00:42:30,520
It’s okay, my little sis.

421
00:42:31,660 --> 00:42:32,600
So…

422
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:38,100
What should I do about Chan?

423
00:42:39,930 --> 00:42:40,800
Fight for her.

424
00:42:42,100 --> 00:42:44,900
If you think you can’t move on from her,

425
00:42:45,780 --> 00:42:48,690
then you need to do everything
so you can go on with her.

426
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:51,800
You didn’t do anything wrong.

427
00:42:52,950 --> 00:42:54,300
You didn’t steal her from anyone.

428
00:42:58,550 --> 00:42:59,400
Come on.

429
00:43:00,590 --> 00:43:03,000
If you think Chan is the one for you,

430
00:43:03,520 --> 00:43:04,700
then go for it.

431
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:27,700
Why did you stop?

432
00:45:37,300 --> 00:45:38,900
I want you to know this.

433
00:45:42,430 --> 00:45:43,900
It’s my job.

434
00:45:47,490 --> 00:45:48,880
What job?

435
00:45:51,700 --> 00:45:53,500
I’ll help you forget her.

436
00:45:57,410 --> 00:45:58,500
From now on,

437
00:46:01,770 --> 00:46:03,700
you will remember only me.

438
00:46:18,750 --> 00:46:19,700
Thank you.

439
00:46:25,260 --> 00:46:26,270
I’m so sorry

440
00:46:27,580 --> 00:46:29,600
for putting you through this.

441
00:46:33,580 --> 00:46:34,780
It’s okay.

442
00:46:38,710 --> 00:46:41,300
Can you hold me like this all night?

443
00:46:44,440 --> 00:46:45,350
Sure.

444
00:46:48,670 --> 00:46:50,500
I will hold you through the night.

445
00:47:06,390 --> 00:47:07,700
I love you.

446
00:47:11,810 --> 00:47:13,180
Even though…

447
00:47:16,170 --> 00:47:18,520
you still don’t love me, it’s okay.

448
00:47:22,370 --> 00:47:24,500
But I will always love you.

449
00:47:29,560 --> 00:47:31,180
I won’t leave you.

450
00:47:43,180 --> 00:47:44,300
Thank you.

451
00:48:03,750 --> 00:48:05,600
I’m sorry.

452
00:48:07,170 --> 00:48:08,500
I’m so sorry.

453
00:48:49,630 --> 00:48:51,580
You are just her sugar baby.

454
00:48:52,190 --> 00:48:53,800
But a sugar baby like me,

455
00:48:54,800 --> 00:48:56,240
I’ve never hurt her.

456
00:48:56,460 --> 00:48:58,600
Chan, do you have any song
you want me to sing?

457
00:48:58,900 --> 00:49:01,160
The song that you sang that night.

458
00:49:01,230 --> 00:49:04,240
About Key? Are you just sleeping with her,

459
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:05,980
or are you serious about her?

460
00:49:07,960 --> 00:49:10,400
I admit it. I still love you, Jay.

461
00:49:10,780 --> 00:49:12,190
I did some digging about you.

462
00:49:12,230 --> 00:49:13,970
You come from a well-known family.

463
00:49:14,010 --> 00:49:16,000
Why did you agree to be Chan’s sugar baby?

464
00:49:16,170 --> 00:49:19,180
If I tell you,
will you get out of Chan’s life?
